\begin_layout Title
Objects First with Java: Correctness Supplement
\end_layout

\begin_layout Author
Anne Mulhern
\end_layout

\begin_layout Chapter*
Introduction
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Programmers should be taught how to write correct programs.
 However, correctness is hard, and teaching correctness is harder still.
 Consequently, instruction in writing programs correctly is too often omitted
 from introductory programming courses.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Students seldom learn how to think about correctness in subsequent courses.
 Software engineering courses are too often devoted to the nebulous practice
 of ``project management'' rather than the discipline of ensuring correctness.
 Courses explicitly devoted to ensuring the correctness of programs focus
 on formal methods.
 Unfortunately, what is taught in these courses is seldom applied elsewhere
 in a curriculum.
 Moreover, the tools used in these courses are often research projects which
 frequently:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Are difficult to install and use.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Work only with an obsolete version of the object language.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Are poorly documented.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Report results that are inscrutable to the novice programmer.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Require a tremendous investment in the study of logic before they can be
 of any use.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Under these circumstances students are likely to learn that program correctness
 is a chimera and to associate the topic of program correctness with tools
 that are nearly impossible to understand and use.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
BlueJ
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "bluej"

\end_inset

 is a Java IDE designed especially for teaching.
 It is quite mature and has an intuitive interface.
 Particularly valuable are its Object Bench, Code Pad, debugger, interface
 with JUnit
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "junit"

\end_inset

, and extension facility.
 Greenfoot
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "greenfoot"

\end_inset

 is an object world for Java which allows a user to develop simple animations
 rapidly.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This work is a supplement to ``Objects First with Java'' by David Barnes
 and Michael K
