\begin_layout Section
Ticket Machine
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Overview
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In this section we present an alternative approach to the design of the
 ticket machine in the BlueJ textbook.
 We alter the design slightly and show how we can make use of testing in
 our design.
 We have built a simple graphical interface to the ticket machine in Greenfoot.
 If the 
\family typewriter
TicketMachine
\family default
 class is implemented correctly, all that is necessary is to place the implement
ation in the Greenfoot 
\emph on
ticket-machine
\emph default
 project and the entire implementation will work appropriately.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Exceptions
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Observe that the 
\family typewriter
TicketMachine
\family default
 constructor and the 
\family typewriter
insertCoin()
\family default
 method make use of exceptions.
 Exceptions are used to signal errors that may occur at run time but can
 not be detected at compile time.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
Exercise:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Open the 
\emph on
ticket-machine
\emph default
